From 83c9d8bbdf49273e64324bfb7bc7b2de4ca7dbbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:19:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] D3D12.X: translated mesh pipelines keep their driver
 blob again

Since 9492f43f, two_pass_mesh_stream names the triangle topology, and
create_mesh_pso added a second PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY subobject next to
the CACHED_PSO one. The runtime refuses a stream with a subobject type
twice (E_INVALIDARG, 0 ms, before the driver), so every MS and GS
pipeline fell to the "without topology" build: no CACHED_PSO, no blob
kept, and each build again (the lab's give-back) was a full compile of
4 - 7 s on the binding thread. In a lab run all 240 such builds logged
"driver blob absent".

create_mesh_pso now adds the topology only to a stream without one.
A stream without one gets exactly the bytes it got before; a stream
with one gets the CACHED_PSO subobject alone, the form
passthrough_mesh_stream_accepts_a_triangle_driver_blob checks on the
GPU. Its blob is then kept in memory (MESH_BLOBS, 256 MB cap) and on
disk (driver\mesh-*.pso, builds of 250 ms or more), as ffb1d17a meant.

Lab (no behaviour change): a per-thread build note records the slowest
driver compile of a build (kind, record, time, blob supplied) and
whether a pipeline of 16 KB or more was compiled without a blob and
none was kept (note_kept: mesh, compute, two-pass compute pass,
graphics), for pso_async::code.

Tests: a_stream_with_its_topology_gets_no_second_one (a runtime that
refuses duplicates: one build, with the blob), the refused-topology
test now checks the note, left_no_blob_only_for_a_big_compiled_
pipeline_without_a_kept_blob, the_build_note_keeps_the_slowest_
compile_until_taken; the GPU blob test also runs on a stream that
names its topology.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
